# The build context for bothy-files and bothy-ops is apps/ (so both images can
# COPY bothy-common/bothy_common). This file makes that context an ALLOWLIST.
#
# Without it, every build would send apps/bothy-web/web/node_modules, the
# audit logs and apps/bothy-ops/secrets (a live cluster token) to the builder.
# A deny-list would have to remember each of those; this cannot forget one.
# bothy-web builds from its own directory and is not affected.
#
# A NEW MODULE must be listed here as well as COPY'd in its Dockerfile, or the
# build fails with "not found" - which is the loud direction to be wrong in.
*
!bothy-common/bothy_common/*.py
!bothy-files/Dockerfile
!bothy-files/requirements.txt
!bothy-files/app.py
!bothy-files/config_api.py
!bothy-files/yamlpatch.py
!bothy-files/policy.toml
!bothy-ops/Dockerfile
!bothy-ops/app.py
!bothy-ops/guard.py
!bothy-ops/control.py
!bothy-ops/kube.py
!bothy-ops/catalog.toml
